th the race and the  under of the individual that is  attempting to rent here although again  they're going to reduce the prominence  of user photographs one of the big  things on Airbnb is they want to make  sure that they know who it is that is  renting and one of the ways they enforce  that is by having you upload a  photograph profile picture sort of like  what you would see on facebook so you  can reduce the prominence but unless you  hide it from the landlord or host all  together I don't exactly know how you  can ensure that there is not going to be  discrimination so uh this is a bit a  pretty big issue that is creating a sort  of black cloud over air B&amp;B in many  areas it's now in 34 thousand cities  it's in a hundred ninety-one countries  it is absolutely huge and when you think  about the types of people the background  and I'm not talking about just race and  gender but also economic backgrounds and  and in so many other areas that could be  renting in different countries etcetera  this is absolutely an issue now let me  tell you another layer of this that is  very interesting I spoke to a friend of  mine over the weekend who is a real  estate and landlord tenant attorney here  in Massachusetts and the laws may be  different from from state to state in  Massachusetts it is not illegal if you  are advertising a room for rent in your  house it is not illegal to reject  individuals based on sexual orientation  for example this would be different than  if you are renting an apartment and it  is truly a uh uh an apartment rental  that would be more governed by law but  if you were renting a room in your house  you may not be able to and this is the  part that was less clear because he the  conversation was interrupted you may not  be able to advertise and I think I'm  pretty sure you can't advertise looking  for a heterosexual roommate for a room  in my house that I am pretty sure is not  allowed but there would be nothing  requiring you to hide if you say you  know really I I want someone who is  heterosexual sharing this room in my  house my understanding based on what my  real estate attorney friend told me is  that is  actually not against the law so this is  really an Airbnb policy that they are  proactively attempting to put in place  non-discrimination not something that is  required by law at least in  Massachusetts when it comes to  individual room rentals something  interesting to keep in mind on my  upcoming trip I'm actually going to be  using air B&amp;B for the first time and I  am NOT renting a room in some guys house  or something like that I'm actually  going through there are some sort of  management companies that will manage a  bunch of air B&amp;B entire apartments and I  very carefully selected one that has  very very high positive views we will  see my sense is that it will be a  positive experience
 

